            <ArticleTitle>4-Bicyclic heteroaryl-piperidine derivatives as potent, orally bioavailable Stearoyl-CoA desaturase-1 (SCD1) inhibitors. Part 1: urea-based analogs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6773-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bmcl.2013.09.096</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0960-894X(13)01182-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new series of urea-based, 4-bicyclic heteroaryl-piperidine derivatives as potent SCD1 inhibitors is described. The structure-activity relationships focused on bicyclic heteroarenes and aminothiazole-urea portions are discussed. A trend of dose-dependent decrease in body weight gain in diet-induced obese (DIO) mice is also demonstrated.</AbstractText>
